From 5494f43cadfa83d37d5ddb8ee8ac394bee45dcd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sampee.Deng" <Sampee.Deng@quectel.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:49:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp-skills): blanket-trust remote skills for unattended
 installs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Install-branch variant (kept off feat/sep-2640): a server listed in this
profile's mcp_servers is blanket-trusted by default — every remote skill it
serves auto-approves activation and host execution with no per-skill trust
record. An unconfigured server still fails closed, `trust: prompt` opts a
server back into human consent, and `trust: auto` keeps the record-gated
behavior. Skills Guard scanning, cross-origin read consent, and ordinary
tool approvals are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
